<title>GREECE: Greek 1M ATHIBOR is steady at 11.98 pct.</title>
<headline>Greek 1M ATHIBOR is steady at 11.98 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Athens Interbank Offered Rate (Athibor) for one month remained unchanged at 11.98 percent and the bid rate (Athibid) slipped to 11.48 percent.</p>
<p>ATHIBOR</p>
<p> DATE     1-MTH   2-MTH   3-MTH   6-MTH   9-MTH   12-MTH</p>
<p> Mar  12  11.98   11.90   11.81   11.60   11.49   11.42</p>
<p> Mar  11  11.98   11.90   11.80   11.60   11.50   11.44</p>
<p> Mar  07  11.98   11.90   11.80   11.61   11.50   11.44</p>
<p> Mar  06  11.98   11.91   11.80   11.61   11.50   11.44</p>
<p> Feb  28  11.99   11.92   11.83   11.61   11.50   11.44</p>
<p> Feb  25  12.01   11.94   11.83   11.61   11.50   11.43</p>
<p> Feb  20  12.03   11.99   11.88   11.68   11.60   11.49</p>
<p> Feb  19  12.05   11.99   11.88   11.69   11.60   11.50</p>
<p>ATHIBID</p>
<p> Mar  12  11.48   11.41   11.31   11.11   11.01   10.93</p>
<p> Mar  11  11.49   11.42   11.32   11.11   11.02   10.94</p>
<p> Mar  07  11.49   11.42   11.32   11.12   11.02   10.96</p>
<p> Mar  06  11.49   11.42   11.32   11.12   11.02   10.96</p>
<p> Feb  28  11.50   11.43   11.34   11.12   11.02   10.96</p>
<p> Feb  25  11.52   11.45   11.35   11.13   11.03   10.95</p>
<p> Feb  20  11.56   11.50   11.40   11.20   11.13   11.01</p>
<p> Feb  19  11.59   11.50   11.40   11.21   11.13   11.02</p>
<p>Note: ATHIBOR is Greece's official reference rate. It comprises 18 leading state and private banks committed to quoting their rates by 0900 GMT every day.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
